---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Shot from '../components/Shot.astro';
import { projects, experience, notes } from '../data/work';

const featured = projects.filter((p) => p.feature);
const more = projects.filter((p) => !p.feature);
const byslug = Object.fromEntries(projects.map((p) => [p.slug, p]));
const when = (p: (typeof projects)[number]) => [p.org, p.years].filter(Boolean).join(', ');
---
<Base>
  <section class="wrap hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <h1 id="hero-title">I design interfaces, then build them all the way down.</h1>
    <p class="intro">I’m Isaac Adelore, a frontend-focused fullstack engineer who also designs. For six years I’ve built products across banking, communication and real-time software, from the Figma file to the database. The interface is where I’m strongest.</p>
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Lagos, Nigeria</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Looking for</dt><dd>Senior frontend or product engineering roles, remote or relocating</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Works across</dt><dd>Product design, frontend architecture, APIs and data</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn solid" href="mailto:adeloreisaac@gmail.com">Email me</a>
      <a class="btn" href="https://linkedin.com/in/adeloreisaac">LinkedIn</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="work-title">Selected work</h2>
      <p>Design, frontend and backend work from the last few years. Internal tools are written up in full, because I can’t show their screens.</p>
    </div>

    {featured.map((p, i) => (
      <article class="feature">
        {p.cover ? (
          <Shot img={p.cover} href={`/work/${p.slug}/`} eager={i === 0}
            sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 820px" />
        ) : (
          <a class="shot brief" href={`/work/${p.slug}/`} tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
            <p class="line">{p.brief!.line}</p>
            <ul>{p.brief!.notes.map((n) => <li>{n}</li>)}</ul>
          </a>
        )}
        <div class="text">
          <p class="kind">{p.kind}</p>
          <h3 class="project-name"><a href={`/work/${p.slug}/`}>{p.name}</a></h3>
          <p class="meta">{when(p) && <span>{when(p)}</span>}<span>{p.role}</span></p>
          <p class="summary">{p.summary}</p>
          <a class="read" href={`/work/${p.slug}/`}>Read the case study</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" id="more" aria-labelledby="more-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="more-title">More work</h2>
      <p>Smaller write-ups, same structure: the problem, what I decided and what came of it.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="more">
      {more.map((p) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`/work/${p.slug}/`}>
            <span class="name">{p.name}</span>
            <span class="summary-sm">{p.summary}</span>
            <span class="tag">{p.kind}</span>
            <span class="where">{when(p)}</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" id="notes" aria-labelledby="notes-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="notes-title">Technical notes</h2>
      <p>Single problems from the work above, and how I solved them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="notes">
      {notes.map((n) => (
        <article>
          <h3><a href={`/work/${n.slug}/`}>{n.title}</a></h3>
          <p>{n.body}</p>
          <p class="from">From {byslug[n.slug].name}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" id="experience" aria-labelledby="exp-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="exp-title">Experience</h2>
      <p>I’ve worked two jobs in parallel for most of my career, so some of these overlap.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="roles">
      {experience.map((r) => (
        <li>
          <span class="years">{r.years}</span>
          <span class="company">{r.company}<span class="role">{r.role}</span></span>
          <span class="note">{r.note}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="about-title">About</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <div>
        <p>I started as a designer who could code and became an engineer who still designs. That means I can sit with a product team on Monday deciding what a screen should do, and be in the API on Thursday making sure it can.</p>
        <p>A clean interface that works properly is the part of the job I enjoy most. Software people depend on to get their work done is the part that keeps me at it. Most of what I’ve built is the second kind: tools a service desk, a data team or a finance lead opens every morning.</p>
        <p>I care about the details people only notice when they’re wrong: what a price change looks like, what an empty screen says, what happens when a request lands on the wrong server, and how a layout holds up on a cheap phone.</p>
      </div>
      <aside>
        <h3>Frontend</h3>
        <p>React, Next.js, Vue, Nuxt, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, TanStack Query, Zustand, Pinia</p>
        <h3>Backend and data</h3>
        <p>Laravel, ColdFusion (CFML), FastAPI, Node, SQL Server, PostgreSQL</p>
        <h3>Design</h3>
        <p>Figma, design systems, UX audits, prototyping</p>
        <h3>Education</h3>
        <p>B.Sc. Computer Science, Covenant University</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
